hey everybody welcome to an only look  into the beta of planet coaster now I  along with a couple of other content  creators got early acces into the beta  in order to make some sneak preview  videos of it and I was figuring for  quite a while of what I actually wanted  to do with this since the time frame I  have to be honest isn't quite large I  only had a couple of spare hours to put  this together before I really don't have  any time anymore and before the game  actually goes public so what I wanted to  do actually is focus on something other  than the coasters which are gonna be  super awesome  there are some great new rides some  great new scenery and great new  additions into the game but one thing  which actually wanted to focus on that I  don't think too many other people are  gonna pick up on are the detailing in  planet coaster the beta comes from what  I've seen with a lot of very small  pieces and a lot very small pieces that  you can recolor and put together in  different ways to make your own kind of  things and what for me is gonna make  this quite a game changer is that with  every new small piece that you get into  into the game the amount of things that  you can do pretty much exponentially  increase and with the new art pieces the  new very narrow pillars and wooden  brackets that kind of stuff in the game  you can actually do a lot to make your  own kind of details to give your own  kind of textures and make really your  own very detailed style of building and  this is what I think also the new beta  is gonna allow for a lot of different  styles and a lot more uniqueness to the  things that people are building so far  many of the builds in planet coaster  still refer back to the same objects  that everybody has there is not that  much free form when it comes to forming  your own balconies and making your own  windows or making your own anything on a  building really and I think the new very  small pieces are gonna be quite a game  changer in this and that's also why I  decided to build the style of building  that I'm building right here I wanted to  pick something very safe because I  didn't have time to blend this all so I  just kind of went  Oh No edit and decided to build a bit of  a French palace kind of stable building  inspired by those simple stable  buildings with an entrance maybe a  couple of towers a few simple  decorations kind of in the style of the  main palace that they're supposed to be  connected to which allows for a small  building but with loads of interesting  details and with the cool palace garden  around it and this is pretty much what I  wanted to settle for and what in the  case of very small details it allows me  to do is actually experiment a bit with  the details that you don't really see in  the game itself but that you can use the  new pieces for so for example the new  textile is art pieces can actually be  used to make your own anything really  but and there are a couple of pretty  small squares rectangles and triangular  and spherical pieces in there which is  so small and so versatile that you can  really make just about any anything out  of it so here I wanted to make a custom  cornice kind of in the style that fits  along with the rest of the building and  on the top of the roof there I also  wanted to put together those pieces to  make some fancy fences with lots of  fancy Peaks on the side as well to make  the building a little bit more  interesting and on the front here where  are we gonna have a small Tower with a  pretty simple spider but still what's  really the most defining feature of the  building I also wanted to play a bit  more with these very small new pieces  but um what I have to say is that before  I open the beta I was actually really  afraid that the new like texture loose  art pieces would not really fit with  building styles like many of the things  that frontier showed them off with and  what I suppose they're really meant for  is making any kind of like cartoony  decoration a thing for example they made  I think stuff like a dragon anything  that you can put together and make very  colorful and very carnival ish looking  but I was actually kind of afraid that  you wouldn't be able to use these pieces  to make custom building pieces and  insert them seamlessly into your  buildings but that's  something which this building sort of  proves otherwise  and that's what I was trying to do here  makes the the the the very free art  pieces together with the regular  building pieces and a mix the textures  and colors a bit make them stand out a  bit and create your own shapes that way  and especially for the cornices here  since I needed I needed some very flat  rectangular shapes and something that  blends into the rest of the scenery  these shapes were very useful for the  roof here I wanted to make a custom roof  and there are some there is a bunch of  new wooden pieces that are super handy  and this one is actually a very small  piece that almost makes this bit of a  roof texture to it if you put a lot of  them together I'm not actually that  worried about the amount of pieces here  the building is still well within the  two thousand pieces at the end not  causing any legs so far so I'm actually  quite happy with that and I'm here just  very quickly putting together the dormer  on the top of the spire here make the  building a bit more fancy I will take  over the top in a little bit but first I  am I wanted to decorate this sides a  little bit and this might just be me but  I'm actually really happy with how the  the very small new pieces as well as the  very narrow new pillars came out because  narrow pillars is something that the  game didn't really have yet but what I  think is actually gonna make quite quite  a big change for me at least since you  can make a lot out of these very narrow  beams you can just make supports out of  them but you can also make these a  victorian sort of galleries and front of  buildings you can make spires definitely  spires there were there's a lot of  pointy bits that you know the pieces  that we had so far were too large and  too bulky for that you can really get  into some more sophisticated smaller  details right now which is also why I  put a ridiculous amount of like as fiery  points on this building as well  and finally on top of the spire here I  wanted to put another pretty large  cornice to finish that off I wasn't  actually that happy with the shape of  the spire I just sort of tried it at  once to see how it would work out and I  wasn't that happy with it but i'm i  think the the top corners kind of shapes  the shapes out of the roof a little bit  more and i'm quite happy actually with  how that looks in the end there's a  bunch of new stuff for windows as well  the new windows are in a much more  generic style i think than the windows  that we had in the game so far which  were quite piratey quite costly and very  spanish or it's just completely modern  but now there are some windows which can  definitely be used in a lot of different  styles there's a lot of new windows and  door pieces that I quite like and over  here especially the dormers came in  pretty handy also I have to say this is  quite a Main Street looking building  even if it's a little bit more European  and many of these pieces can definitely  be made to make some very Disney asked  Main streets just something that I think  is very interesting and as one of the  lost parts of making the building I  wanted to get some dormers on the top of  the windows here just because that's  pretty much the only way to make this  roof a little bit more interesting most  of the detail in this building is really  in the roof I wanted to keep the walls  quite flat and have just all of these  different points and fences and  decorations on the roof and just to make  them come out a bit more I wanted to put  some dormers on them here as well which  are very simple I didn't want to take  time to really make these dormers too  interesting but um I'd least wanted to  get some dormers in there and these  quickly made dormers worked out pretty  nicely there  and finally it really comes down to the  detailing of the building to make it  come to life a bit and there's bunch of  new lanterns and stuff that you can hang  on the sides of balls and roofs and  that's why I quickly did there there's  also the robe which is supposed to be  used for the Western theme but it has a  French flag on it and I was like hey why  not might as well try it so I put that  on the balcony on the front and then the  last thing that I wanted to do which  isn't really related to the building  itself but really to making the building  look the way that it's gonna look in  some kind of context make the quick  simple Palace Gardens and I am not sure  if I really got this correctly but it  kind of seemed to me like the paths were  flowing a bit more easily though it's  probably just me I didn't actually try  it that much in lost alpha but I was  actually quite surprised in any case how  well the parts were doing with coming  together here and I think being able to  get the parts together to make some  actual larger plasters without curbs in  the middle an interesting new option in  the paths section is that you can  actually remove the kerb of a part which  is pretty cool because I actually didn't  quite like how if you put different  parts on the side of each other you have  curbs in the middle that was one of the  things that worked me about the pass  system but that's something that's a  thing of the past now which is quite  nice and also there are all of these new  textures which I'm really happy with  those and they are a lot more washed out  and generic and I think also a lot more  versatile than the part textures that we  had before so that's a very big  improvement and yeah especially in this  case since it has that old rustic brick  texture and the the gravelly Palace card  and texture it fits perfectly for what  I'm trying to go for here so there was  no reason not to use the new textures  for the pass here also of course I kinda  want to show them off as well now  finally I was struggling with these  lamps a bit as happy as I am with these  new lights because so far we didn't have  any  I like antique light posts yet the only  light post that we had was the modern  one and these look really good I was  trying to decorate them for a bit but  that didn't cover that well you can  always hang some planters on it or put  some extra Victorian decorations on them  but in this case I didn't have the  patience anymore and when it gets throw  it into the foliage because there are a  lot of new trees and I really like the  way that they look they're also a bit  more like that the colors are quite  different than what we had so far so far  many of the foliage items have very  similar colors which resulted in not  that very landscape when it comes to the  color of foliage but these the new trees  will definitely help make parks look a  lot more lush and I'm very happy with  that anyway that's just about it for  this time-lapse I hope you all enjoyed  and I hope you're looking forward to  seeing the beta it is awesome and I wish  you all a lot of fun with trying it
 

